{"kind":"event","event_id":8374,"event_uid":"01M2PV84QYHKN2T2H4FRB4M8KQ","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.commented","project_id":33,"project_uid":"01M2HSJCAB4WXJ7C6XEG23B869","project_name":"popmechanic-tinyapp-fixture","issue_id":346,"issue_uid":"01M2PV4YH2PCBTAEJHB6NWYHD8","issue_short_id":"yhd8","actor":"impl:1@run-28","hlc_physical_ms":1789620654846,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"553fb80c6d1dfbad5020ac2462d58e32079cfd48d6796184818200fd0f94cfc8","payload":{"comment_uid":"01M2PV84QXFV54SFF9PAKMNXQ5","author":"impl:1@run-28","body":"Approach: TagsInput.tsx modelled on DueInput.tsx — design-system Input, id `tags-<rowId>`, placeholder `tags, comma-separated`, aria-label `Tags for <todoText>`, layout-only `w-40 shrink-0`. Local useState(tags) + mirror useEffect on [tags]; onChange writes local text only; onKeyDown Enter preventDefault -> setTodoTags(store, rowId, text) (imported from ./storeData, since Store.tsx does not re-export it) -> setText(normalizeTags(text)), passed through unconditionally so the empty clear branch reaches the store. Mount in TodoItem directly after DueInput, before the Delete button. Loosen the three text-input-count pins of type-due-date.test.ts to the #due-<N> ids they meant. type-tags.test.ts is the peer's exam; I do not write it.","created_at":"2026-09-17T04:50:54.845228358Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-17T04:50:54.846Z"}
